hadiths[47]{hadithnumber,text}:
"493","Ghatif ibn al-Harith said that a man came to Abu 'Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah\nwhile he was in pain and asked"
"494","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"495","'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn Sa'id reported that his father said"
"496","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet"
"497","Abu Hurayra said"
"498","Khalid bin al-Rabi"
"499","It is reported by Ayeshah that the Prophet said"
"500","It is narrated by Ayeshah (ra) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"501","I was seriously ill at Makkah and the \nProphet visited me. I said to him """"Messenger of Allah"
"502","It is narrated by Abdullah bin Amr that Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"503","Anas bin Maalik has reported that the Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"504","Abu Hurayrah said that fever presented itself before the Holy Prophet (ﷺ). It said to him"
"505","Abu Hurayrah said that he did not like any illness more than fever because it went into each of his limbs. And"
"506","It is reported by Abu wail that someone said to Abu Nuhaylah (when he was ill)"
"507","Ata bin Abu Rabah said that Ibn Abbas asked him if he would like him to show him a woman who would go to paradise. So"
"508","It is reported by Ibn Jurayj that Ata said to him"
"509","Abu Hurayrah reported the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying"
"510","It is narrated by Jabir that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say"
"511","either\nyou will be killed and I will leave you to Allah or you will win and I\nwill be content. Beware of having your portion presented to you and then\nyou do not agree with it. Accept it"
"512","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri reported that he came to the Messenger of Allah"
"513","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah said"
"514","Usama ibn Zayd reported that a child of one of the daughters of\nthe Messenger of Allah"
"515","Ibrahim ibn Abi 'Abla said"
"516","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"517","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah"
"518","Jabir said"
"519","'I asked you for food and you\ndid not feed Me. He (His slave) will say"
"520","Abu Sa'id reported that the Prophet"
"521","to visit the sick"
"522","Three of the Banu Sa'd related from their father that the Messenger\nof Allah"
"523","Abu Qilaba reported from Abu'l-Ash'ath as-San'ani that Abu Asma'\nsaid"
"524","Abu Bakr ibn Hazm and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir were some people\nfrom the mosque who visited 'Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Rafi' al-Ansari. They\nsaid"
"525","'Ata' said"
"526","Anas reported that a Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet"
"527","Every body is given the prayer to arise healthy among his people"
"528","Ibn 'Abbas reported that the Prophet"
"529","Nafi' reported that when Ibn 'Umar visited someone who was ill"
"530","'Amr ibn Sa'id said"
"531","'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As said"
"532","Al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah al-Ansari said"
"533","'Abdullah ibn Abi'l-Hudhayl said"
"534","Zayd ibn Arqam said"
"535","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad reported that one of the Companions of Muhammad\nlost his eyesight and people visited him. He said"
"536","Anas said"
"537","Abu Umama reported that the Prophet"
"538","Ibn 'Abbas said"
"539","Ar-Rabi' ibn al-Hasan said"
